Project: Eigen, template library for linear algebra: matrices, vectors, numerical solvers, and related algorithms
URL: https://libeigen.gitlab.io/
Repository: https://gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen
License: MPL-2.0. A few files carry permissive third-party notices: BSD-3-Clause
for the Intel MKL/BLAS/LAPACKE/PARDISO bindings (used only with EIGEN_USE_MKL,
EIGEN_USE_BLAS or EIGEN_USE_LAPACKE, which Natron doesn't define, or with
PardisoSupport, which nothing includes) and for AlignedBox::transform, a
permissive BSD-style notice for the half-float conversion routines in Half.h,
and Apache-2.0 for BFloat16.h. There is no LGPL code: Amd.h and
SimplicialCholesky_impl.h were relicensed to MPL2 upstream (1dc1677d5, before
3.4.0), IncompleteLUT.h was relicensed to MPL2 by its author, nothing includes
Core/util/NonMPL2.h, and every module Natron uses compiles with
-DEIGEN_MPL2_ONLY.
Upstream version: 3.4.1 (tag 3.4.1, commit d71c30c47858effcbd39967097a2d99ee48db464)
Local modifications: none

The tree under Eigen/ is upstream 3.4.1, unmodified. eigen-update.sh refreshes
it from the 3.4.1 git tag and checks that the tag is still commit
d71c30c47858effcbd39967097a2d99ee48db464. That Eigen/ directory is identical to
the one in the release archive eigen-3.4.1.tar.bz2 (sha256
8bb7280b7551bf06418d11a9671fdf998cb927830cf21589b394382d26779821, the checksum
recorded by MacPorts; Eigen publishes none). The script also deletes any
CMakeLists.txt under Eigen/; 3.3.x shipped some, 3.4.x has none, so that step
is only defensive.

Earlier revisions were taken from Blender's extern/ folder and carried a
patches/blender.diff plus a note about an OpenMP fix for MSVC2015. Neither was
present in the tree: comparing the vendored 3.3.7 against upstream 3.3.7 found
no differing file, and the patch did not apply to that version either. Both
have been dropped rather than carried forward as something they were not.
